[21.957099, "o", "\r\n"]
[25.016609, "o", "transport tunnel (socks5 127.0.0.1:1088)\r\n  reachable         yes\r\n  known-open        open      reply 0x00         0.7ms\r\n  known-closed      error     no reply           0.3ms   <- expected closed\r\n  blackholed        filtered  no reply        3054.3ms\r\n\r\n  fidelity          open_only\r\n  The known-closed destination produced no usable reply code (the proxy\r\n  may have timed out or closed the connection, which is what OpenSSH's\r\n  `ssh -D` does), so closed and filtered cannot be distinguished.\r\n\r\n  to record this, add to [transports.tunnel]:\r\n      fidelity = \"open_only\"\r\n"]
[27.519457, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2;36m# open_only: closed and filtered are indistinguishable through it. The scan says so\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[27.921135, "o", "\u001b[2;36m# up front, and records error rather than guessing closed.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
